I've left out the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and this change would give it outbound network access that the graph doesn't declare. The fetch would also send the digest's data to an external host while its result is discarded, which is an exfiltration pattern rather than enrichment. To add it properly, update the graph's `with` clause for this node, then regenerate. The node below uses only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Mark every considered id as seen, kept or not. Only ids not already
        // present are counted as newly recorded.
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in published.considered.iter() {
            if state_rw::get(id).is_none() {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

